### Problem

State is fragmented across three stores with no defined ownership:

| State            | `_session_store` | `ExecutionContext` | `TrainingOrchestrator.state` |
| ---------------- | ---------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------- |
| schema           | ✔                | ✔ (after FIX-10)   | ✔ (phase_results)            |
| target override  | ✔                | ✔ (user_overrides) | ✔ (phase_results slot)       |
| model selection  | ✔ (after FIX-04) | ✔ (after FIX-10)   | ✔ (phase_results)            |
| training signals | ✗                | ✔ (after FIX-10)   | ✔ (phase_results)            |

No code defines **which store is authoritative** when they diverge. This creates hidden bugs when a user updates the schema override mid-session.

### Ownership Rules (Deterministic)

```
ExecutionContext = PRIMARY (authoritative, persistent via session_manager)
_session_store   = CACHE (ephemeral refs only: lazy data, raw hashes, scaler path)
TrainingOrchestrator.state = EXECUTION-ONLY (internal phase book-keeping, not read outside)
```

Mapping:
